    "common_form_notes": "Extremely widely stocked in plate, bar, angle, channel, and I-beam sections. Most common structural steel in North America.",
    "usage_frequency": "Common",
    "notes": "Low-carbon structural steel per ASTM (American Society for Testing and Materials) A36/A36M. Hot-rolled condition. Yield and tensile strengths are ASTM A36 minimum specified values; as-supplied material typically exceeds these minimums. Equivalent to EN (European Norm) S275 and similar grades. Excellent weldability. Not suitable for service below approximately -30 °C without impact testing. Shear strength derived from von Mises criterion: UTS (ultimate tensile strength)/√3 = 400/1.732 ≈ 231 MPa. Melting point is solidus (1425°C); liquidus 1540°C (metalzenith-a36)."
  },
  "typical_usage": "Structural frames, beams, columns, gussets, brackets, machine bases, weldments, and general fabrication. The default steel for structural and general-purpose work where high strength is not required.",
